course: dictionary
lesson: 9611
title: Strive: trying very hard
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To strive means to try very hard to do or get something, and to keep trying for a long time. «We strive for excellence» means we keep working hard, again and again, to do our very best.
explain: Strive can also mean to struggle or fight against something. «Why strive? why struggle?» Here the two words sit close together: strive shows the effort, and struggle shows how hard that effort is.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like hard, best, for, against and long time often sit near strive. Swap in try hard and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: Strive means to try very hard, often over a long time.
fact: Strive can also mean to struggle or fight against something.
fact: «We strive for excellence» is a motto you may see in school, meaning we keep working to be the very best.
fact: Strive is a verb, so it shows an action: you strive, she strives, we are striving.
fact: The past forms are strove or strived, and striven or strived, so you can say «They strove» or «They have striven».
exercise: «She strives to do her best in every spelling test.» What does strives mean here? | Stops trying and gives up | *Tries very hard over a long time | Forgets all about the test | Sleeps through the test
exercise: «The knight strove against the dragon for three days.» Find and copy the word that shows he struggled hard. | dragon | knight | three | *strove
exercise: The school motto says, «We strive for excellence.» What does it ask pupils to do? | Sing loudly in assembly | *Work hard and keep trying to do their best | Give up when work is hard | Stay silent all day
test: «Why strive? why struggle?» What is the best meaning of strive here? | To shout loudly | To give up quickly | To sleep | *To try very hard
test: Ravi says strive means just sit about and wait. Why is he wrong? | Strive means to wait for the bus | Strive means to be lazy | Strive means to be happy | *Strive means to try very hard and keep going
exam: Which sentence uses strive to mean struggle or fight against something? | The shop strives to open at noon every day | The sky strove to turn green on Tuesday | I strive to finish my book in the car | *The firefighters strove against the flames to save the house
